Generated changelog for v1.9.0

--- Technical ---
### Changed

- This release will integrate the complete M9 - Frontend Redesign milestone into `main` and add the v1.9.0 release notes. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- This release will reintroduce inline citation badges that were first built in #207, now over the sanitized Markdown answer instead of plain text. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- This release will make the most likely next step in `SuggestedNextSteps` a button that runs it. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- This release will add a keyboard-first command palette that opens over any page, anchored on the power-user `Ctrl/Cmd+K` chord. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- This release will apply the target status to the card up front (optimistically) and reconcile with the server afterwards. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- This release will replace `AssignTicketDialog` and `ChangeStatusDialog` with inline popovers anchored to the header actions. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- This release will anchor citations to the answer text and render inline badges with hover preview. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- This release will inject the agent roster into the system prompt of every chat request. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- This release will enforce the grounding check via `tool_choice` once `IRagRetrievalContext` holds passages and no check has run. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- This release will make `Theme/DesignTokens.cs` the single source for the palette, spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic chip colours. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- This release will wrap the title `<a>` in a `board-card__title-row` div to ensure `-webkit-line-clamp` applies. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- This release will target the panel through `::deep .assistant-chat` to restore its intended padding and layout. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- This release will give the `Category` column a `140px` width and render its header with the same uppercase style as its neighbours. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- This release will add two rules to the chat system prompt to enforce write honesty and avoid needless confirmation. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- This release will convert every timestamp in the `BuildTicketPrompt` to the user's local timezone before the model sees it. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- This release will return `IsError: true` for the catch branch of `search_knowledge_base`, distinguishing it from the `unavailable` degradation path. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- This release will score grounding by meaning using a semantic comparison of answer sentences and passages. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))
